# Per-checkout personal files, each named by the convention of the agent that
# reads it, and none of them the project's. `AGENTS.override.md` is the one
# worth being deliberate about: it replaces `AGENTS.md` at the same level
# rather than adding to it, so committing one would silently swap this
# project's canonical instructions out from under every agent that follows
# the convention.
CLAUDE.local.md
.claude/settings.local.json
AGENTS.override.md

# Anything else you keep in your own checkout -- notes, scratch directories,
# translations of these documents -- belongs in `.git/info/exclude`, or in the
# global excludes file `git config --global core.excludesFile` names, and not
# here. A rule in this file is the project telling every contributor what to
# hide; those are yours to decide.
